    "designNotes": "6 units numbered 8-13 in the CED (continuing the AP Physics C: Mechanics numbering 1-7). Unit weights, topic codes/titles, class periods, skill weights and exam format are from the posted CED (read 2026-10-20). Exam: hybrid digital; Section I 42 MC, 85 min, 50%; Section II 4 FRQ, 95 min, 50% (Mathematical Routines 10 pts, Translation Between Representations 12 pts, Experimental Design and Analysis 10 pts, Qualitative/Quantitative Translation 8 pts; 40 pts total). Four-function, scientific or graphing calculator allowed on both sections. Calculus-based; Practice 2 MC weighting (2.A 25-30%) is higher than the algebra-based courses. Per-topic and per-sub-keyword skills are an ALTON editorial mapping (one skill per sub-keyword chosen by kind and content), not the CED's per-topic suggested skills. Sub-keywords, kinds, requires and estLessons are ALTON editorial designs, not CED content. Topic titles are the CED's where read from the CED course-at-a-glance; where the extracted text was truncated they are close paraphrases."
